**Important** — Structural refactor mislabeled as "fluid cards", zero test coverage

**What:** This 572-line change (the largest in the MR) isn't a pure CSS tweak — it replaces a single CSS-branched table with a full `isMobile ? <cards> : <table>` conditional render, extracting 8+ helper functions (`renderSiteActions`, `renderSeoScore`, `renderGeoScore`, `renderStatus`, `renderPlan`, etc.) so both layouts share the same logic. The refactor itself checks out as behavior-preserving on inspection, and owner-only permission gates were verified preserved identically in both branches — but it's materially higher-risk than "fluid project cards, wrapping header/action buttons" implies, and `ClientDetailView` has no test file at all, before or after this change.

**Why it matters:** A future edit to either branch (mobile or desktop) has nothing to catch a regression that only shows up in the other branch — there's no automated signal today.

**Recommendation:**
```tsx
// Add a smoke test covering both render paths, e.g.:
describe('ClientDetailView', () => {
  it('renders desktop table layout at desktop width', () => { ... });
  it('renders mobile card layout at mobile width', () => { ... });
});
```
Also worth calling out this refactor explicitly in the MR description as a distinct, higher-risk change rather than bundling it under "fluid project cards."

Confidence: 85/100 | Found by: MR Analyst (OmniForge)

**Minor** — Unlinked magic-number duplication

**What:** The new mobile toggle offset hardcodes `288` (`isOpen ? 288 : 10`), which is a duplicate-with-offset of the drawer's own mobile width `280` defined a few lines later (`width: isMobile ? 280 : '18%'`). The two numbers aren't linked by any shared constant. The sibling component `SiteSection.tsx` (touched in this same commit) does this correctly — its toggle position is derived via `calc(${t.width} * 17/18)` from the same token that sizes its drawer.

**Why it matters:** If the mobile drawer width (`280`) ever changes, this toggle position will silently drift out of alignment with no compiler or lint warning.

**Recommendation:**
```tsx
// Derive from the same value used for the drawer width, mirroring SiteSection.tsx:
const mobileDrawerWidth = 280;
// ...
left: isMobile ? (isOpen ? mobileDrawerWidth + 8 : 10) : (isOpen ? '17%' : '10px'),
// ...
width: isMobile ? mobileDrawerWidth : '18%',
```

Confidence: 70/100 | Found by: Codebase Reviewer (OmniForge)

